WEBVTT

00:07:59.470 --> 00:08:01.922
So the question is
how to solve it collectively.

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:04.107
When Vivek was surgeon general,

00:08:04.131 --> 00:08:06.666
he decided to tackle it
in his own office.

00:08:06.690 --> 00:08:10.264
One of his first efforts
was to try what everyone tries:

00:08:10.288 --> 00:08:12.329
picnics and happy hours.

00:08:12.353 --> 00:08:14.946
And the results were
what they usually are.

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:18.668
VM: People end up talking about
what they have most in common,

00:08:18.692 --> 00:08:19.852
which is work.

00:08:19.876 --> 00:08:21.034
So it can be helpful,

00:08:21.058 --> 00:08:24.276
but not nearly as helpful,
I think, as we hope they can be.

00:08:24.300 --> 00:08:26.161
So what we did in contrast is,

00:08:26.185 --> 00:08:29.556
we decided after doing these
to try something different.

00:08:29.580 --> 00:08:32.295
AG: Wait a minute.
So you killed happy hour?